commit e50cab6d1f9abd2d4ecc5af8af6fed5c1c030485
Author:     Brendan Abolivier <brendan@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Wed Jul 16 20:38:33 2025 +0200
Commit:     Brendan Abolivier <brendan@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Wed Jul 16 20:38:33 2025 +0200

    Bug 1957975 - Part 1: Refactor simple EWS callbacks interface into one. r=edicharry

    This patch focuses on "simple" EWS listeners, i.e. listeners that only have a
    success (and optionally error) callback. The idea is to replace all of them with
    a single standardised interface, with only a couple of implementations defined
    in a single place.

    A second optional interface is also introduced so that implementations needing
    errors to be fed back to the consumer can do so in a flexible way. Note the
    error callback for this second interface changes from previous ones by
    propagating the actual `nsresult` from the error (when available) rather than a
    variant of `IEwsClient::Error`. This latter enum was introduced with the belief
    that authentication failures would be handled on the C++ side of things, which
    isn't true (see bug 1971540). Using an `nsresult` directly means a better
    integration with the rest of Thunderbird.

    These implementations use lambda functions to 1) allow them to be as generic as
    possible, and 2) make it so all of the code that deals with a specific operation
    lives in the same place, and improve readability and maintainability.

    I have a few next steps in mind for future patches (because this one is large
    enough as it is):

    * Make `IEwsClient` return the stored Exchange Server version for the server, so
      we can get rid of the boolean parameter in success callbacks.
    * Make the more complex callbacks implement `IEwsFailibleOperationListener` to
      standardise error handling in `ews_xpcom`.
    * Move the more complex callbacks to `EwsListeners.{h,cpp}` to declutter the
      files they're currently defined in (maybe also make them use lambdas? I'm not
      sure yet at this point).

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D258237

